WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.420
We're currently waiting on the Supreme Court's
decision, really two decisions about Donald

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.410
Trump's tax returns, and I'm hoping to have
news about that either later on in today's

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:12.710
program or if not, we'll talk about it tomorrow
on the Friday show with you.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:17.130
But we do have a new Supreme Court decision
to talk about that came out yesterday.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:21.250
And if you've been following the Supreme Court
for the last couple of weeks, you might be

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:27.750
aware that we had some reasonable decisions,
some correct decisions from my perspective,

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.270
from the Supreme Court over the last few weeks.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.160
But we did not get that yesterday.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:40.040
The Supreme Court has sided seven to two with
the Trump administration to allow employers

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:48.780
to deny access to employees of free contraceptive
coverage if the reason for wanting to deny

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.570
free birth control is religious in nature.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:58.000
And this is I mean, listen to the the the
seven to two decision.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:06.530
The seven majority each had varied, not all
the same reasons why they were with the majority,

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:11.480
but the decision in and of itself is a huge
win for the religious right.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.100
And it is a loss for Obamacare as well.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.830
It's a loss for secularism.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:21.100
And it's certainly at least a win that the
Trump administration can claim now that this

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:27.070
is one of the few wins that the Trump administration
can claim as part of a bigger discussion about

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:33.140
what is the case to be made that Trump has
accomplished anything and should be Iraq reelected?

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:36.020
Not not not what I almost said.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:38.530
But that is really a case that Donald Trump
has to make.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.560
That's not a case for me to make.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.409
But this is at least something that went his
way.

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:45.830
The DOCA decision not going his way.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.740
LGBT discrimination decision not going his
way.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:55.150
And the Trump administration has actually
tried a number of different ways to hurt Obamacare

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:57.140
with different regulations.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:05.500
One such regulation is that if you are a religious
based employer, you now will be able to say

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.200
our employees, people who have health insurance
under.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:15.990
But as a result of working for us, they will
no longer be able to get free birth control.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:22.180
One of the things that Obamacare said was
that birth control is free to the patient.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:29.270
They must have full coverage of contraceptive
services and products as part of their health

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:31.150
insurance plans.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:36.340
Houses of worship, including churches, temples
and mosques, were exempt from that requirement

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:37.390
from the get go.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.390
Some people weren't.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.450
We're not aware of that.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:44.830
But a lot of nonprofit groups like schools,
which could be religiously affiliated or based

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:49.980
hospitals, which could be religiously affiliated
or based, were not exempt.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:55.320
If you worked for them, they had to through
their insurance coverage that you were offered

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.760
as an employee, had to offer contraceptive
services at no cost.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.760
Some of them objected right away and they
said that goes against our religious beliefs.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:04.760
How are we?

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:12.970
It is a violation of our freedom of religion
to say we must allow we must provide no cost

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:19.300
at to the patient, of course, contraceptive
services when we don't believe that those

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:23.940
should be something people avail themselves
of on the basis of our religious beliefs.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:27.730
In came the Trump administration and they
said, we agree with the religious employers

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:35.610
requiring birth control coverage without cost
burdens, the free exercise of religion.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:41.220
They put in place some exemption rules were
employers can say we opt out, their employees

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:46.840
can still get birth control, but it wouldn't
be free of a cost through their health insurance

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:47.840
plan.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.500
Now, since the Affordable Care Act requires
it.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:55.739
What that meant in practice is that the states
where people live would have to pay.

00:03:55.739 --> 00:03:59.550
And states like Pennsylvania and New Jersey
said, hold on a second.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:06.239
If employers are not required to provide this
through their health insurance, we have to

00:04:06.239 --> 00:04:07.239
pay for it.

00:04:07.239 --> 00:04:10.780
And that's not fair to us, said Pennsylvania
and New Jersey.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:15.340
A lower court agreed with Pennsylvania and
New Jersey.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:19.269
That is the decision that has now been reversed
by the Supreme Court.

00:04:19.269 --> 00:04:24.990
The seven to two vote in the Supreme Court
had Ruth Bader Ginsburg and Sonia Sotomayor

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.819
as the only dissenters.

00:04:27.819 --> 00:04:34.169
The majority said these restrictions put in
place by the Trump administration are okay.

00:04:34.169 --> 00:04:41.979
And for me, the major takeaway and what I
want to remind you of is that this is another.

00:04:41.979 --> 00:04:47.090
Explanation another way to remind ourselves
that health insurance should not be tied to

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:48.650
employers, period.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:50.050
That that's my takeaway.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:53.330
And of course, you can fight the legal battle.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:56.219
And that's exactly what the Trump administration
did.

00:04:56.219 --> 00:05:01.139
But at a higher level, health insurance tied
to employers is the wrong direction.

00:05:01.139 --> 00:05:06.439
And in terms of how far this goes, there is
a slippery slope question here as well.

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:12.039
I mean, if you look at, I don't know, Christian
Science, Christian Science is very much against

00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:14.360
all sorts of medical care.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:19.960
Would antibiotics be a legit exemption if
they are religiously based?

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:24.490
If if Christian Science says, listen, we run
this big Christian Science, you know, reading

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:30.149
room or whatever they call it, and we don't
want to provide antibiotics with it.

00:05:30.149 --> 00:05:32.899
We don't want antibiotics to be so accessible.

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:33.899
Would that be valid?

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:36.379
I mean, how far does this go now?

00:05:36.379 --> 00:05:40.419
The estimates are that somewhere between 70
thousand and one hundred and twenty six thousand

00:05:40.419 --> 00:05:44.719
women are going to lose contraceptive coverage
as a result of this decision.

00:05:44.719 --> 00:05:50.460
And what this really is is pointing back to
is this is an administration, the Trump administration,

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:52.499
that has lost on policy.

00:05:52.499 --> 00:05:54.749
Trump was going to repeal and replace Obamacare
failed.

00:05:54.749 --> 00:05:55.979
He was going to build the wall failed.

00:05:55.979 --> 00:05:57.009
He was going to fix this.

00:05:57.009 --> 00:05:58.009
Fix that.

00:05:58.009 --> 00:05:59.009
Fix it.

00:05:59.009 --> 00:06:00.849
He's failed on on essentially everything.

00:06:00.849 --> 00:06:02.629
They are now fighting a culture war.

00:06:02.629 --> 00:06:04.319
Remember that Donald Trump is not religious.

00:06:04.319 --> 00:06:06.550
This is merely pandering.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.520
And it is a win on paper for Donald Trump.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:13.990
How much of a big deal he makes out of this
win remains to be seen.

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:15.319
But this is a culture war.

00:06:15.319 --> 00:06:19.960
If you look at the last six weeks, you know,
the right loves to accuse the left of fighting

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.259
a culture war.

00:06:21.259 --> 00:06:27.199
The reality is that it's Trump who, faced
with losing on just about every policy issue,

00:06:27.199 --> 00:06:31.729
is now talking about we've got to fight these
radical Marxists.

00:06:31.729 --> 00:06:36.690
Mark, there's barely any Marxists and certainly
none in positions of power in the United States.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:38.219
This is about our heritage.

00:06:38.219 --> 00:06:41.699
Visa V monuments and the Confederate flag.

00:06:41.699 --> 00:06:43.379
And it's about free speech.

00:06:43.379 --> 00:06:45.229
These are culture war type battles.

00:06:45.229 --> 00:06:51.300
And again, this you're not really damaging
Obamacare in the sense of removing it the

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.009
way he wants to do.

00:06:53.009 --> 00:06:56.710
You're just making life more difficult for
seventy thousand to one hundred and twenty

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:57.939
six thousand more women.

00:06:57.939 --> 00:07:03.240
And Trump, who is not religious, continues
to pander to the religious right through these

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.229
types of arguments and regulations.

00:07:05.229 --> 00:07:08.110
So that's what it all is really about.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:12.090
There is stunning hypocrisy as well, because
you block access to birth control.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:16.749
But then do you do you provide parental leave,
paid parental leave when the baby is born?

00:07:16.749 --> 00:07:21.509
Many, many employers do not in this, certainly
not mandated to, et cetera, et cetera.

00:07:21.509 --> 00:07:23.119
I think you get the idea.

00:07:23.119 --> 00:07:28.340
But at least on paper, it is a win for the
Trump administration, a win that they desperately

00:07:28.340 --> 00:08:43.439
need because these wins are so few and far
between.

